1
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,541
一个音被按下。然后，它开始消失。
A note is struck. Then it begins to disappear.

2
00:00:13,791 --> 00:00:17,751
坂本龙一用一生，倾听这段消失。
Ryuichi Sakamoto spent his life listening to that disappearance.

3
00:00:23,551 --> 00:00:27,163
一九五二年，他出生在东京。
He was born in Tokyo in 1952.

4
00:00:27,413 --> 00:00:34,044
少年时，他迷恋德彪西，甚至相信自己是德彪西转世。
As a boy he was so taken with Debussy that he believed he was his reincarnation.

5
00:00:34,294 --> 00:00:37,934
在东京艺术大学，他学习作曲，
At Tokyo University of the Arts he studied composition,

6
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:41,073
也钻研电子音乐与民族音乐。
and delved into electronic and ethnic music.

7
00:00:47,273 --> 00:00:51,883
一九七八年，他与细野晴臣、高桥幸宏，
In 1978, with Haruomi Hosono and Yukihiro Takahashi,

8
00:00:51,903 --> 00:00:54,994
组成黄色魔术交响乐团（YMO）。
he formed Yellow Magic Orchestra (YMO).

9
00:00:55,244 --> 00:01:01,358
合成器与音序器，把东京的电子流行乐送往世界。
Synthesizers and sequencers carried Tokyo's electronic pop to the world.

10
00:01:10,858 --> 00:01:16,448
一九八三年，他为电影《圣诞快乐，劳伦斯先生》作曲，
In 1983 he scored the film Merry Christmas, Mr. Lawrence,

11
00:01:16,468 --> 00:01:18,605
也在片中出演。
and acted in it too.

12
00:01:18,855 --> 00:01:23,455
《末代皇帝》为他赢得奥斯卡最佳原创配乐，
The Last Emperor won him the Oscar for Best Original Score;

13
00:01:23,475 --> 00:01:27,001
《遮蔽的天空》又带来金球奖。
The Sheltering Sky brought a Golden Globe.

14
00:01:27,251 --> 00:01:32,895
五声音阶的旋律，在西方管弦乐里找到了回声。
Pentatonic melodies found their echo in the Western orchestra.

15
00:01:39,295 --> 00:01:42,206
他从不属于单一的风格。
He never belonged to a single style.

16
00:01:42,456 --> 00:01:46,166
二〇〇一年，他与莫雷伦鲍姆夫妇，
In 2001, with Jaques and Paula Morelenbaum,

17
00:01:46,186 --> 00:01:49,446
在里约热内卢，若宾的故居里，
in Jobim’s house in Rio de Janeiro,

18
00:01:49,466 --> 00:01:53,121
用若宾的钢琴，录下专辑《家》（Casa）。
he recorded the album Casa on Jobim’s own piano.

19
00:01:53,371 --> 00:01:58,103
钢琴、大提琴与人声，向波萨诺瓦致意。
Piano, cello and voice, in homage to bossa nova.

20
00:02:05,303 --> 00:02:08,783
与德国艺术家阿尔瓦·诺托合作时，
Working with German artist Alva Noto,

21
00:02:08,803 --> 00:02:12,712
他把钢琴削减成稀疏的音符，
he pared the piano down to sparse notes,

22
00:02:12,962 --> 00:02:16,182
与正弦波和电子噪音交错。
interlaced with sine waves and electronic noise.

23
00:02:16,202 --> 00:02:18,845
寂静，也成了乐谱的一部分。
Silence became part of the score.

24
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:30,189
他前往北极圈，录下冰川融水的声音。
He travelled to the Arctic Circle to record the sound of melting glaciers.

25
00:02:30,439 --> 00:02:36,189
二〇一一年海啸之后，他弹奏了被海水浸泡过的钢琴，
After the 2011 tsunami he played a piano drowned in seawater,

26
00:02:36,209 --> 00:02:39,369
说，那是大自然在为它调音。
and said nature was retuning it.

27
00:02:39,619 --> 00:02:42,009
二〇一七年的专辑《async》，
In 2017, the album async

28
00:02:42,029 --> 00:02:46,228
让每个声音，按照自己的时间呼吸。
let every sound breathe in its own time.

29
00:02:53,628 --> 00:02:58,558
二〇二三年一月十七日，他七十一岁生日那天，
On January 17, 2023, his 71st birthday,

30
00:02:58,578 --> 00:03:02,159
专辑《12》发行，像是一本声音日记。
he released 12, like a diary written in sound.

31
00:03:02,409 --> 00:03:06,023
同年三月，他离开了这个世界。
That March, he left this world.

32
00:03:06,273 --> 00:03:11,537
他最喜欢的一句话是：艺术长久，人生短暂。
His favorite phrase: Ars longa, vita brevis. Art is long, life is short.

33
00:03:18,537 --> 00:03:21,213
音会消失，余韵长存。
The note fades. Its resonance remains.

